UNDERPOWERED -- NO FINDING EITHER WAY (rho=+0.836).

  The sweep covers 0.086 of the breadth axis and 0.239 of the depth axis, where 1.000 is the retain oracle. Peak depth 0.332 means the unlearned model erased about 33% of what retraining-without-the-data achieves.
  That is a corner of the plane, and the question -- whether depth gives way as breadth grows -- is a question about the shape of a curve. This curve has no room to bend.

  Raise --epochs until forgetting approaches the oracle (watch the per-epoch forget_nll against the utility floor), then re-run.

